selection techniques to  capture the cumulative effect of a small  effect size snips  which is variable in complex diseases  then by building a machine learning  model for each chosen subset of snips  and evaluating their accuracies the  power of each approach is to be assessed  and by revealing the genetic basis of ad  we will manage to build more protective  models for alzheimer's disease  this is an overview of our proposed  framework first our data set was  obtained from national alzheimer's  coordinating center it consists of  364 unique symbols each sample contains  almost  380 thousand snips  the framework applies a pre-processing  stage according to specific quality  control steps to ensure the rata meets  certain criteria such as missing grade  tests and imputation the minor allele  frequency test snip encoding to  represent snips as numeric values  we divided the snips into four batches  according to their b values  and to evaluate the b value snip  selection technique the only snips  that should be used as features  are the ones in batch zero as its snips  b value are  10 to the power of minus five  while the other batches were used in  testing the second selection technique  and assessing the interaction technique  we consider a higher number of snips to  capture the cumulative effect however we  have to keep the number of snips  comparable with the sample size to  assure that the training model will not  overfit the data hence working with the  finite number of data symbols in a high  dimensional feature space we needed to  eliminate some features using a feature  selection method before using another  model to fit the data here we try to  propose  machine learning based feature selection  techniques that rely on different  considerations and the phenotype  association we search for a feature  selection technique that uses the least  number of features to avoid overfitting  and achieve the highest accuracy as well  the feature selection techniques we  tried are mutual information and linear  svc with l1 penalty  as illustrated in the left graph the  best score was achieved by battery 2  that is consist  of  441 snips  whose b value of all of them raised to  10 to the power by the three  bet two achieves higher accuracy than  than  said zero and one using both linear and  rbf kernel with support with support  vector machine model the second approach  is that combine both the value technique  and machine learning approach achieved  better predictive capacity using both  linear and rbf kernels  we mainly depend on neutral information  and machine learning based selection  technique as illustrated in the right  graph the best accuracy achieved  is  93 and have  using 300 snips we can also note that  the higher the number of features we set  the better the achieved accuracy which  supports the first hypothesis of  interaction however the model accuracy  starts to decrease at some point which  may be due to some false positive snips  that we're taking into consideration in  the model  we investigated the ad correlation with  the 300 snips that we computationally  used in decision making to find out if  they are experimentally supported  using nomad database we found that  180 sniffs of them are located in 152  genes by looking them up in literature  we found out  that of the  152 genes there are 104 unique genes  related to alzheimer's disease or other  related diseases as well as 11 ad  correlations with the sniffs themselves  pathway enrichment analysis revealed  that there are 146 pathways associated  with these 300 snips with 26 correlated  pathways to neural system  we try to use setoscape to do network  analysis we graphed the snips along with  the affected genes  nodes represented both the snips and  genes in a network and edge between any  snip and genes indicate the biological  association  then for focused analysis  the nodes with more than three edges are  filtered which means  this genes affected by more than three  snips  looking those seven interesting genes  have we found  the following three genes  are experimentally verified to be  related to alzheimer's disease  to conclude the application of genomic  association studies in case control  setups have resulted in plethora of  significant genetic variants associated  with complex diseases phenotypes  integrating machine learning with the  feature selection technique i would  perform zabi value statistical method  finally our  are to increase the sample size under  examination in terms of having more  patients and to apply the same pipeline  to symbols taken from egyptian patients  with alzheimer's disease because  this neb  brand differentiable  because the snipper and differ  because the snip print differs with  different bibulation we are looking for  creating a personalized health reward  service which enables egyptians to  obtain detailed information and rewards  based on their genome and take  appropriate action  that's it and thank you
 

